# Feature Technical Specification Standard

<introduction>
This reference provides guidance for creating standardized feature technical specifications. It ensures comprehensive documentation of implementation details, interfaces, and considerations for integrating new features into existing codebases.
</introduction>

<context>
- Implementing a new feature based on requirements
- Planning the technical implementation of a feature
- Documenting changes to existing components
- Defining integration points for a feature
- Specifying performance optimizations and error handling
</context>

<template_structure>
A feature technical specification should follow this structure:

1. **Introduction** - Purpose and overview of the feature
2. **Requirements Reference** - Link to originating requirements
3. **Architectural Context** - How the feature fits into the system
4. **Implementation Components** - New and modified components
5. **Configuration** - Parameters, validation, and storage
6. **Data Flow** - Acquisition, processing, and output
7. **Implementation Details** - Core logic, performance, error handling
8. **Integration** - How the feature integrates with existing system
9. **Testing Strategy** - Approach for testing the feature
10. **Implementation Phases** - Sequence for implementation
11. **Constraints** - Technical limitations and boundaries
12. **References** - Links to relevant documentation
13. **Examples** - Code examples showing implementation
14. **Critical Points** - Essential aspects of the implementation
</template_structure>

<examples>
<example>
# Feature Technical Specification: Tool Offset Gathering

<introduction>
This feature enables the Mitsubishi-Citizen MTConnect adapter to collect, process, and report tool offset data from Mitsubishi M700/M70 series CNC controllers. It provides real-time tool offset information for monitoring and analysis in MTConnect-compatible applications.
</introduction>

<configuration>
<parameters>
| Parameter | Type | Default | Valid Range | Description |
|-----------|------|---------|-------------|-------------|
| tool_offset_enabled | boolean | false | true/false | Enables/disables tool offset gathering |
| max_tool_offsets | integer | 20 | 1-100 | Maximum number of tool offsets to gather |
</parameters>
</configuration>

<implementation_details>
<core_logic>
- Determine number of available tool offset sets via MEL API
- Collect tool offset data in batches to maintain performance
- Convert tool offset values to appropriate units for MTConnect
</core_logic>
</implementation_details>

<critical_points>
- ALWAYS validate configuration parameters before use
- IMPLEMENT batched collection for performance optimization
- HANDLE axis-specific data collection through appropriate MEL API calls
</critical_points>
</example>
</examples>

<critical_points>
- ALWAYS link to the originating requirements document
- SPECIFY both new components and modifications to existing components
- DOCUMENT configuration parameters with proper validation rules
- INCLUDE detailed data flow from acquisition to output
- HIGHLIGHT performance optimizations for critical operations
- DEFINE clear integration points with existing systems
- OUTLINE comprehensive testing strategy including edge cases
- PROVIDE concrete code examples where appropriate
- ENSURE all critical implementation considerations are documented
- SPECIFY implementation phases for complex features
</critical_points>

